Receiver-Relative Signaling — RRS-001

Version 1.0 · Markdown · 15 KB

Core law

A signal has no universal behavioral meaning. Its effects depend on the receiver’s beliefs, objectives, capabilities, environment, and history.

Includes a 10-step operator, input/output schemas, counterfactual modeling, second-order consequences, eight tests, and Pantheon integration instructions.

